---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { profile } from '../data/profile';
import { education } from '../data/experience';
import { mentors } from '../data/mentors';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About — Prateek Mittal"
  description="Personal biography, academic mentorship at MNNIT Allahabad and Yale, industry experience, and perspectives of Prateek Mittal."
>
  <div class="max-w-5xl mx-auto px-6 sm:px-8 py-8 sm:py-12 space-y-12 sm:space-y-14">
    
    <!-- Page Header -->
    <div class="space-y-2 border-b border-warm-200 dark:border-warm-800 pb-6">
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-serif font-medium text-warm-900 dark:text-warm-50 tracking-tight">
        About Me
      </h1>
      <p class="text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400 font-sans text-sm">
        Background, research trajectory, the mentors who guided me, and personal perspectives.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- 2-Column Responsive Layout -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8 lg:gap-10 items-start">
      
      <!-- Main Content: Justified Long-Form Narrative in Editorial Serif -->
      <div class="lg:col-span-8 space-y-5 font-serif text-[17px] text-stone-800 dark:text-stone-200 leading-[1.85] text-justified hyphens-auto">
        <p>
          I have always felt that mathematics, social conscience, and poetry are not separate endeavors, but three dialects of the same quiet search for clarity.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-medium text-warm-900 dark:text-warm-50 pt-3 text-left">
          Academic Research & Collaborations
        </h2>
        <p>
          My research is rooted in problems where differential geometry and statistical theory help us interpret biological complexity. Primarily, this work has evolved in close collaboration with the <strong>Vision Exploration & Data Analytics (VEDAs) Lab</strong> at <strong>Motilal Nehru National Institute of Technology (MNNIT) Allahabad</strong> under the continuous mentorship of <strong>Dr. Joohi Chauhan</strong>, who has guided my academic research since my undergraduate days at Thapar Institute.
        </p>
        <p>
          Starting in 2025, <strong>Dr. Prabal Pratap Singh</strong> joined as a close collaborator across multiple initiatives. Together, our work has led to five accepted contributions at <strong>MICCAI 2026</strong> (including three oral presentations and the competitive MICCAI Society Travel Grant) and theoretical work on adaptive stratified subsampling published in <strong>Transactions on Machine Learning Research (TMLR)</strong>.
        </p>
        <p>
          In 2024, my early research journey was deeply enriched through a remote research collaboration with <strong>Dr. David van Dijk</strong> at <strong>Yale University</strong>, contributing to <strong>BrainLM</strong> (ICLR 2024)—a foundation model trained on 6,700 hours of whole-brain fMRI recordings to decode human cognitive states from functional neuroimaging. That experience fundamentally shaped how I think about large-scale foundation modeling in biology.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-medium text-warm-900 dark:text-warm-50 pt-3 text-left">
          Industry Decision Science & Clinical Operations
        </h2>
        <p>
          In industry, I work as an AI Decision Science Analyst within <strong>Accenture Strategy & Consulting</strong>'s AI & Data ecosystem in Gurugram, contributing to backend development, problem framing, and enterprise transformation workflows.
        </p>
        <p>
          Prior to Accenture, I spent two formative years at <strong>Dr. Lal PathLabs</strong> as Data Scientist – Assistant Manager. My time there was heavily shaped by senior leadership: I received strategic IT and enterprise transformation guidance from <strong>Mr. Munender Soperna (Group CIDO)</strong> and cloud engineering mentorship from <strong>Gaurav Sharma</strong>. On clinical systems, I worked under <strong>Dr. Reena Nakra (Principal Director – Lab Operations & CSO)</strong> and <strong>Dr. Nimmi Kansal (National Head – Clinical Chemistry)</strong> to ensure that patient-facing RAG assistants and unified health-score algorithms were rigorously grounded in diagnostic validity and Indian population reference intervals.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-medium text-warm-900 dark:text-warm-50 pt-3 text-left">
          Grassroots Roots & Ethical AI
        </h2>
        <p>
          Long before publishing machine learning papers, my most humbling education occurred during my Bachelor’s degree in Computer Engineering at Thapar Institute. I spent four years with <strong>Pratigya Abhiyan</strong>, an initiative providing free education to children of daily-wage laborers and migrant families. Rising from volunteer educator to Academic Head, sitting on concrete floors teaching children taught me empathy, listening, and that brilliance exists everywhere—opportunity does not.
        </p>
        <p>
          That grassroots realization led me to found the <strong>Foundation for Ethical AI in Healthcare (FEAIH)</strong>—a Section 8 initiative aimed at addressing the regulatory, clinical, and liability gap for clinical algorithms in India (published in <em>Health Policy and Technology</em>).
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-medium text-warm-900 dark:text-warm-50 pt-3 text-left">
          Poetry & The Quiet Hours
        </h2>
        <p>
          When work is done, I write poetry in Hindi and English. My writing revolves around themes of <em>भीतर का ठिकाना</em> (the inner refuge) and <em>क्षीर-नीर विवेक</em> (the classical philosophical ideal of separating essence from noise). It is how I stay grounded, thoughtful, and human.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Right Sidebar: Portrait & Quick Facts -->
      <div class="lg:col-span-4 space-y-6">
        <div class="rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-warm-200 dark:border-warm-800 bg-warm-50 dark:bg-warm-900/60 p-4 shadow-sm space-y-4">
          <div class="aspect-[4/4.5] w-full rounded-xl overflow-hidden bg-warm-200 dark:bg-warm-800">
            <img
              src="/images/prateek.png"
              alt="Prateek Mittal"
              class="w-full h-full object-cover object-top"
            />
          </div>

          <div class="space-y-2 text-xs font-sans text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300 divide-y divide-warm-200/80 dark:divide-warm-800/80">
            <div class="pt-1">
              <span class="text-stone-400 block">Name</span>
              <span class="font-medium text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">Prateek Mittal</span>
            </div>
            <div class="pt-2">
              <span class="text-stone-400 block">Location</span>
              <span class="font-medium text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">Gurugram & Faridabad, India</span>
            </div>
            <div class="pt-2">
              <span class="text-stone-400 block">Current Industry</span>
              <span class="font-medium text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">AI Decision Science @ Accenture</span>
            </div>
            <div class="pt-2">
              <span class="text-stone-400 block">Research Collaboration</span>
              <span class="font-medium text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">MNNIT Allahabad (VEDAs Lab)</span>
            </div>
            <div class="pt-2">
              <span class="text-stone-400 block">Formative Research</span>
              <span class="font-medium text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">Yale BrainLM (2024)</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- 30-Min Discussion Booking Box -->
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-warm-200 dark:border-warm-800 p-4 text-xs font-sans space-y-2.5 bg-warm-100/60 dark:bg-warm-900/40">
          <h3 class="font-serif font-medium text-sm text-warm-900 dark:text-warm-50 flex items-center gap-1.5">
            <span>Schedule a 30-Min Call</span>
          </h3>
          <p class="text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-400 leading-relaxed">
            Interested in discussing research collaborations, healthcare AI ethics, or decision science? Pick a convenient time on my calendar:
          </p>
          <a
            href="https://calendly.com/prateekmittal154/30min"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="inline-flex items-center justify-center gap-1.5 w-full py-2 px-3 rounded-lg bg-brick-600 hover:bg-brick-700 text-white font-medium text-xs transition-colors shadow-sm"
          >
            <svg class="w-3.5 h-3.5" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M8 7V3m8 4V3m-9 8h10M5 21h14a2 2 0 002-2V7a2 2 0 00-2-2H5a2 2 0 00-2 2v12a2 2 0 002 2z" />
            </svg>
            <span>Book 30-Min on Calendly</span>
            <span>&rarr;</span>
          </a>
        </div>

        <!-- Contact Box -->
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-warm-200 dark:border-warm-800 p-4 text-xs font-sans space-y-2">
          <h3 class="font-serif font-medium text-sm text-warm-900 dark:text-warm-50">Direct Email</h3>
          <p class="text-stone-500">
            For academic queries, preprint discussions, or notes:
          </p>
          <a
            href="mailto:prateekmittal154@gmail.com"
            class="text-brick-600 dark:text-brick-500 font-medium hover:underline block pt-1"
          >
            prateekmittal154@gmail.com &rarr;
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>

    <!-- Mentors & Advisors Grid on About Page -->
    <section class="border-t border-warm-200 dark:border-warm-800 pt-10 space-y-6">
      <div class="space-y-1 border-b border-warm-200 dark:border-warm-800 pb-3">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-serif font-medium text-warm-900 dark:text-warm-50">
          Mentors & Academic Advisors
        </h2>
        <p class="text-xs text-stone-500 font-sans">
          The researchers, clinicians, and technology leaders who have shaped my thinking, research rigor, and engineering ethics.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3 gap-5">
        {mentors.map((m) => (
          <div class="p-4 rounded-xl border border-warm-200/90 dark:border-warm-800/90 bg-warm-50/50 dark:bg-warm-900/40 hover:border-brick-500/40 transition-colors space-y-2.5 flex flex-col justify-between">
            <div class="space-y-1.5">
              <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-[11px] font-sans">
                <span class="text-brick-600 dark:text-brick-500 font-medium uppercase tracking-wider text-[10px]">
                  {m.category === 'academic' ? 'Academic Mentor' : 'Industry Guidance'}
                </span>
                <span class="text-stone-400">{m.period}</span>
              </div>

              <h4 class="font-serif text-base font-medium text-stone-900 dark:text-stone-100">
                {m.name}
              </h4>
              <p class="text-xs font-sans text-stone-500 dark:text-stone-400 font-medium">
                {m.role} · <span class="italic">{m.affiliation}</span>
              </p>

              <p class="text-xs font-sans text-stone-600 dark:text-stone-300 leading-relaxed pt-1 text-left">
                {m.relationship}
              </p>
            </div>

            <div class="pt-2 text-xs font-sans flex items-center justify-between border-t border-warm-200/60 dark:border-warm-800/60">
              {m.linkedin && (
                <a
                  href={m.linkedin}
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener noreferrer"
                  class="text-brick-600 dark:text-brick-500 hover:underline font-medium inline-flex items-center gap-1"
                >
                  <span>LinkedIn Profile</span>
                  <span>↗</span>
                </a>
              )}
              {m.website && (
                <a
                  href={m.website}
                  target="_blank"
                  rel="noopener noreferrer"
                  class="text-stone-400 hover:text-stone-700 dark:hover:text-stone-200"
                >
                  Lab Website ↗
                </a>
              )}
            </div>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

  </div>
</BaseLayout>
